---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "Can LKProfessionals build a hotel or accommodation booking website?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Booking websites can be designed around the property's room, availability, enquiry, reservation and payment workflow.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can a hospitality website support direct bookings?",
    answer:
      "Yes. The website can provide a direct reservation or enquiry path depending on the booking model and systems used by the property.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can booking or payment systems be integrated?",
    answer:
      "Where suitable APIs or supported integration mechanisms exist, booking engines, payment providers, messaging platforms and other operational systems can be connected.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can guest reminders and confirmations be automated?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Predictable communications such as confirmations, arrival instructions and selected reminders can often be automated once the workflow and communication rules are defined.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can LKProfessionals help reduce dependence on third-party booking platforms?",
    answer:
      "We can improve the property's own website, direct booking journey, search visibility and digital marketing. Third-party channels may still remain useful, so the goal is usually better channel balance rather than assuming they should be removed entirely.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can the website support multiple properties or room types?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Multi-property, room-type and related structures can be designed into the website or custom application where required by the operating model.",
  },
];
---

<section class="hospitality-faq">
  <div class="site-container hospitality-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>Hospitality FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Questions before sending another guest to a third-party platform.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="hospitality-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .hospitality-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .hospitality-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(17rem, 0.7fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
  }

  .hospitality-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .hospitality-faq h2 {
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .hospitality-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .hospitality-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .hospitality-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .hospitality-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .hospitality-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
